# Architecture Overview

This document contains a high-level architecture diagram (Mermaid) and short descriptions of the main components.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
  %% Users and Clients
  user[User] --> browser[Web App<br/>(Browser / Mobile)]

  %% Edge
  browser --> cdn[CDN]
  cdn --> lb[Load Balancer]

  %% Ingress / API Gateway
  lb --> ingress[API Gateway / Ingress]

  %% Core Services
  ingress --> auth[Auth Service<br/>(OAuth / JWT)]
  ingress --> apiA[API Service A<br/>(Orders)]
  ingress --> apiB[API Service B<br/>(Products)]

  %% Data plane
  apiA --> db[(Primary DB<br/>Postgres)]
  apiB --> db
  apiA --> cache[(Cache<br/>Redis)]
  apiB --> cache
  apiA --> mq[(Message Queue<br/>Kafka / RabbitMQ)]
  mq --> workers[Background Workers]
  workers --> db
  apiA --> storage[(Object Storage<br/>S3)]
  apiB --> ext[External APIs]

  %% Infrastructure
  subgraph infra [Kubernetes Cluster]
    ingress
    apiA
    apiB
    workers
  end

  infra --> monitoring[Monitoring & Logging<br/>(Prometheus / Grafana / ELK)]
  infra --> tracing[Distributed Tracing<br/>(Jaeger / Zipkin)]

  %% CI/CD & Source
  repo[Source Repo (GitHub / GitLab)] --> ci[CI/CD<br/>(GitHub Actions / GitLab CI)]
  ci --> infra

  %% Users of events / async consumers
  extConsumer[External Consumers] --> mq

  %% Optional: Admin / Ops
  admin[Admin / Console] --> ingress
  admin --> monitoring

  %% Styling (optional)
  classDef infraStyle fill:#f8f9fb,stroke:#cfe2ff;
  class infra infraStyle;
  class db,mq,cache,storage fill:#fff7e6,stroke:#f5c26b;
```

## Components (brief)
- User / Web App: Browser or mobile client.
- CDN & Load Balancer: Edge caching and traffic distribution.
- API Gateway / Ingress: Routing, rate limiting, authentication entry point.
- Auth Service: Issues/verifies JWTs or handles OAuth flows.
- API Services: Small, focused microservices (Orders, Products, etc.).
- Primary DB: Relational datastore (Postgres) for transactional data.
- Cache: Low-latency reads (Redis).
- Message Queue: Event-driven / async communication (Kafka / RabbitMQ).
- Background Workers: Process jobs, consumers of message queue.
- Object Storage: S3-compatible storage for blobs, assets, backups.
- External APIs: Third-party integrations.
- Kubernetes Cluster: Hosts services, scaling and deployment boundary.
- Monitoring & Tracing: Prometheus, Grafana, ELK, Jaeger for observability.
- CI/CD & Repo: Source control and pipeline to build, test, deploy.

## How to render
- Use a Markdown renderer that supports Mermaid (e.g., VS Code + Mermaid Preview, GitHub (if enabled), or Mermaid Live Editor).
- To export an image, paste the mermaid block into the Mermaid Live Editor or use tooling like mermaid-cli.

## Notes
- This is a generic, adaptable overview. Replace services/names with specifics from your stack (e.g., MySQL instead of Postgres, or GCP services).
